.TH NFLOG2SYSLOG 8 "2026-09-30" "nflog2syslog" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
nflog2syslog \- forward kernel NFLOG packets to syslog as JSON
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nflog2syslog
[\fB\-\-nflog\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR] [\fB\-\-dest\fR \fIIP:PORT\fR] [\fB\-\-proto\fR \fIudp|tcp\fR]
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nflog2syslog
binds to a Linux kernel NFLOG group (netfilter's NFLOG target) over a
netlink socket, dissects every logged packet into protocol layers
(IPv4/IPv6, TCP/UDP, ICMP, ARP, GRE, DNS, DHCP, NTP, SNMP and more), and
forwards one JSON object per packet to syslog — the local syslog socket by
default, or a remote server via UDP or TCP.
.PP
The receive path is decoupled from the syslog sink through bounded queues:
a stalled syslog server causes counted, reported drops instead of blocking
the kernel socket. The netlink socket buffer is enlarged with
SO_RCVBUFFORCE (falling back to SO_RCVBUF without CAP_NET_ADMIN).
.PP
Requires the CAP_NET_ADMIN capability (the NFLOG group bind needs it
anyway). Statistics (processed, queue drops, kernel drops, sink errors)
are written to stderr every \fB\-\-stats\-interval\fR seconds when nonzero.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-nflog\-group " " \fIGROUP\fR
NFLOG group to listen on; must match the \fB\-\-nflog\-group\fR of your
iptables/nftables rules. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-\-dest " " \fIIP:PORT\fR
Remote syslog destination. Empty (default) sends to the local syslog socket.
.TP
.BR \-\-proto " " \fIudp|tcp\fR
Transport for the remote syslog server. Ignored without \fB\-\-dest\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-copy\-range " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of packet bytes the kernel copies per logged packet.
Default: 1024.
.TP
.BR \-\-rcvbuf " " \fIBYTES\fR
Netlink socket receive buffer size. Default: 8388608 (8 MiB).
.TP
.BR \-\-queue\-size " " \fIN\fR
Capacity of the internal pipeline queues. Default: 8192.
.TP
.B
Copy every JSON message to stdout as well (useful under systemd/journald).
.TP
.BR \-\-local\-syslog
Copy every JSON message to the local syslog socket as well.
.TP
.BR \-\-stats\-interval " " \fISECONDS\fR
Seconds between stderr statistics reports; 0 disables. Default: 10.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/nflog2syslog
Default configuration read by the systemd unit
(\fInflog2syslog.service\fR): DEST, PROTO, NFLOG_GROUP, STATS_INTERVAL.
.SH SIGNALS
.B SIGTERM / SIGINT
trigger a graceful shutdown: the NFLOG group is unbound and queued
messages are drained to the configured sinks before exiting.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iptables\-extensions (8),
.BR syslog (3),
.BR systemd (1)
